    {
      "id": "27f11c63-2033-48f2-b339-c77184d9e636",
      "text": "I found my way to a busy kebab shop and got a chicken stew with rice (15 QAR, $4) and mutton and chicken kebabs (20 QAR, $5.50). The mutton was incredible. (Why don't we get that in the US? We only have lamb). I chatted with two Chinese travelers in their mid 30s who sat at my same table. They were architects who came to Qatar to see several buildings famous for their architectural style. I ended the night by getting some fresh Za'atar Chapati street food (3 QAR, ~$0.8).",
      "type": "text"
    },
